# scrolltender.lic
=begin
      author: Fizzleworth
        name: scrolltender
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, scroll infusion, infuse, unlock, scroll, 714
    requires: fizzfuse.lic 2.6 (and eherbs.lic, go2.lic)
     version: 1.0.0
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Runs ;fizzfuse over a whole container of scrolls, unattended.

  Usage:
    ;scrolltender                      your scrollsack (;vars set scrollsack=...): check every
                                       scroll, infuse the ones that can take more charges, and
                                       put each back in the scrollsack. Unlocks nothing.
    ;scrolltender <source> <target>    unlock and infuse every scroll in <source>; the finished
                                       ones go in <target>. For other characters' scrolls.
                                       ;scrolltender cloak kit
                                       ;scrolltender "leather case" suede.sack

  With no arguments, for each scroll:
    - ;fizzfuse check, back in the scrollsack.
    - A spell with "the potential to add <anything but no>" is worth infusing, so
      ;fizzfuse infuse. With "no charges" (vibrant: "no additional time") on every spell, or
      no message at all (locked), it's left where it is.

  With two, for each scroll:
    - ;fizzfuse unlock, again and again until every spell is unlocked. Only then
      ;fizzfuse infuse, because a scroll can't be unlocked any more once it has been infused
      (a plain ;fizzfuse infuses after the first wave that fails).
    - A wave that "shakes violently" is tried again, unlock_tries times in a row. One that
      "shakes slightly" and a white aura on the stone are final: in the logs nothing unlocked
      after either (12 of 12 waves).
    - Whatever did unlock is infused and goes in <target>. A scroll with nothing unlocked
      stays in <source>, and the summary says so. Scrolls that are already unlocked and full
      go straight to <target>.

  Unlocking can destroy the scroll and kill you. In all the logs (May to November 2026) the
  stone exploded on 3 of 677 waves: one killed Fizzleworth from full health (11/13), the other
  two left him stunned and bleeding. After an explosion this kills fizzfuse (which would go on
  waving at nothing), runs ;eherbs, and carries on with the next scroll. Dead, or still hurt
  after eherbs, it stops. That only happens unlocking, so the no-argument run doesn't risk it.

  It also kills a fizzfuse that hasn't got anywhere for stall_limit seconds (waiting for mana
  and walking to the shops don't count), puts the scroll back and goes on; two scrolls in a row
  ending badly stop the run. fizzfuse makes its own runestones as usual (20,000 silvers in the
  local bank). If it's running, go4invoker is paused until the end, so it doesn't walk you off
  with a scroll in your hand.

  Game text this relies on, all from Fizzleworth's logs:
    check         "As the runestone passes over the scroll, you sense:" then
                  "   (712) Cloak of Shadows with a few charges remaining and the potential to
                   add many charges."  (locked: the line ends at "remaining.")
    unlocked      "The smooth stone vibrates and begins to glow.  You sense that the scroll has
                   somehow been altered."
    failed        "The smooth stone shakes violently, but nothing happens."  / "shakes slightly"
    ruined        "The smooth stone is momentarily surrounded by a dim (or bright) white aura."
    explosion     "The smooth stone explodes in a flash of blue flame as it passes over the a
                   scrap of luminous papyrus, destroying it."
    infused       "...The scroll glows dimly for a moment."
    locked for    "  The scroll is momentarily surrounded by a bright white aura." and "The
    good          scroll glows dimly for a moment, and then grows cold."  The charges are kept.
    full          "...The mana dissipates."
=end

module ScrollTender
  VERSION = '1.0.0'

  # ---- the knobs (methods, so an edit takes effect on the next run)
  # How many ;fizzfuse unlocks in a row may unlock nothing (each one is a wave that shook
  # violently) before the rest of the scroll's spells are given up on.
  def self.unlock_tries
    3
  end

  # The most times to run ;fizzfuse infuse on one scroll. One is enough unless the link
  # slipped or infuse_safe is on and an infusion was a struggle.
  def self.infuse_tries
    3
  end

  # Seconds fizzfuse may go without the game saying anything that counts as getting somewhere.
  def self.stall_limit
    180
  end

  # With less mana than this, fizzfuse is taken to be waiting for mana.
  def self.mana_wait
    60
  end

  # Run eherbs before the next scroll when bleeding or below this percent health, and stop the
  # run if you're still bleeding or below stop_below afterwards.
  def self.heal_below
    75
  end

  def self.stop_below
    50
  end

  # ---- game text (see the header)
  STATUS_START = /^As the .*stone passes over the .+, you sense:/
  STATUS_SPELL = /^\s*\((?<num>\d+)\) (?<spell>.+?) with (?<left>.+?) remaining(?: and the potential to add (?<add>.+?))?\.?\s*$/
  UNLOCKED     = /You sense that the .+ has somehow been altered/
  SHOOK        = /shakes violently, but nothing happens/
  SHOOK_LITTLE = /shakes slightly, but nothing happens/
  STONE_AURA   = /^\s*The .*stone is momentarily surrounded by a \w+ white aura/
  SCROLL_AURA  = /^\s*The .* is momentarily surrounded by a \w+ white aura/
  EXPLODED     = /stone explodes in a flash of .+ as it passes over/
  WENT_COLD    = /glows dimly for a moment, and then grows cold/
  INFUSED      = /glows dimly for a moment\./
  STRAINED     = /^.*You strain to harness the mana/
  FULL         = /The mana dissipates\./
  NO_MANA      = /^You don't have enough mana/ # gswiki; not in the logs
  INJURED      = /^You can't make that dextrous of a move/
  # fizzfuse waving or infusing with nothing in its hand
  EMPTY_HANDED = /^You must have something in your left hand to wave|^You wave your .* around\.$|lose your focus/
  # making a runestone
  RUNE_WORK    = /^You rummage through|Sold for [\d,]+ silvers|you draw the .+ rune on|shatters into twinkling dust/
  NO_SILVER    = /already spent what you're trying to withdraw|don't have that much|You have no account|insufficient/i
  LINKED       = /form a link with it|^You feel your link to the .+ slip/

  CLOSED    = /^(?:That|The .+) is closed/
  LOOK_DONE = Regexp.union(/^Total items|^There is nothing in|^In the .+? you see|^I could not find|^What were you referring to/, CLOSED)
  OPEN_DONE = /^You open|^You carefully|^You unfasten|^That is already open|^I could not find|^What were you referring to/
  GET_DONE  = /^You (?:remove|get|grab|pull|take|pick up|retrieve|slip|already have)|^Get what|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|^You need a free hand|^You can't|^You are still stunned/
  PUT_DONE  = /^You (?:put|place|slip|tuck|add|drop|carefully roll)|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|won't fit|^That is closed|too (?:full|heavy|large)|^You are still stunned/
  SWAP_DONE = /^You swap|^You have nothing to swap/

  # same scrolls as scrollinv and fizzfuse
  NOUNS   = %w[scroll vellum parchment papyrus palimpsest paper].freeze
  EXCLUDE = /\A(?:a |an |some )?(?:birth certificate parchment|amnesty parchment)\z/i

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- small stuff
  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[scrolltender] #{text}"
  end

  def self.bold(text)
    _respond "<pushBold/>[scrolltender] #{text}<popBold/>"
  end

  def self.count(number, noun)
    "#{number} #{noun}#{'s' unless number == 1}"
  end

  def self.wait_for(seconds)
    end_time = Time.now + seconds
    until yield
      return false if Time.now > end_time
      sleep 0.2
    end
    true
  end

  # put, not fput (fput can take an unrelated line for the reply; see fizzpure)
  def self.collect(action, done, timeout: 5)
    lines = []
    Script.current.clear
    put action
    end_time = Time.now + timeout
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line
        lines << line
        if line =~ /^(?:\.\.\.w|W)ait ([0-9]+) sec/
          sleep [Regexp.last_match(1).to_i - 0.5, 0.3].max
          put action
          end_time = Time.now + timeout
          next
        end
        break if line =~ done
      else
        sleep 0.1
      end
      break if Time.now > end_time
    end
    lines
  end

  def self.right_id
    GameObj.right_hand.id&.to_s
  end

  def self.left_id
    GameObj.left_hand.id&.to_s
  end

  def self.in_hand?(item)
    right_id == item.id.to_s
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- containers
  # "leather case", "leather.case", "my kit", "kit": the last word is the noun and every other
  # word starts a word of the name (same as sing_all / orb_check / fizzpure)
  def self.matches?(obj, name)
    words = name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '').split(/[\s.]+/)
    return false if words.empty? || obj.nil? || obj.id.nil?

    obj.noun.to_s.casecmp?(words.last) && words[0..-2].all? { |word| obj.full_name.to_s =~ /\b#{Regexp.escape(word)}/i }
  end

  # worn only: fizzfuse needs both hands
  def self.find_container(name)
    Array(GameObj.inv).find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
  end

  def self.open_up(container)
    lines = collect("open ##{container.id}", OPEN_DONE, timeout: 3)
    @opened |= [container] if lines.any? { |line| line =~ /^You (?:open|carefully|unfasten)/ }
  end

  # a fresh LOOK IN, so the IDs are live. Opens it if it's closed.
  def self.look_in(container)
    waitrt?
    lines = collect("look in ##{container.id}", LOOK_DONE)
    if lines.any? { |line| line =~ CLOSED }
      open_up(container)
      collect("look in ##{container.id}", LOOK_DONE)
    end
    sleep 0.3
    Array(container.contents)
  end

  def self.scroll?(obj)
    NOUNS.include?(obj.noun.to_s.downcase) && obj.name.to_s !~ EXCLUDE
  end

  # the name to give fizzfuse's --cont, quoted so a two-word name stays one argument
  def self.cont(name)
    %("--cont=#{name}")
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- moving scrolls
  # into the right hand, left hand empty
  def self.take(item)
    3.times do
      return false if dead?

      wait_for(60) { !stunned? }
      waitrt?
      next unless clear_hands(except: item)

      collect("get ##{item.id}", GET_DONE, timeout: 4) unless in_hand?(item) || left_id == item.id.to_s
      wait_for(2) { [right_id, left_id].include?(item.id.to_s) }
      if left_id == item.id.to_s
        collect('swap', SWAP_DONE, timeout: 3)
        wait_for(2) { in_hand?(item) }
      end
      return true if in_hand?(item)
    end
    false
  end

  def self.put_away(id, container)
    2.times do
      wait_for(60) { !stunned? }
      waitrt?
      lines = collect("put ##{id} in ##{container.id}", PUT_DONE, timeout: 4)
      return true if wait_for(2) { ![right_id, left_id].include?(id.to_s) }

      open_up(container) if lines.any? { |line| line =~ CLOSED }
    end
    false
  end

  # anything but the scroll itself is fizzfuse's (a runestone, the brush, ...): the infusesack
  def self.clear_hands(except: nil)
    [left_id, right_id].compact.each do |id|
      next if except && id == except.id.to_s
      return false unless put_away(id, @infusesack)
    end
    true
  end

  # Wherever a run that went wrong left it (hand, infusesack, source, target), back to source.
  def self.bring_home(item)
    return false if dead?

    [left_id, right_id].compact.each { |id| put_away(id, id == item.id.to_s ? @source : @infusesack) }
    return true if holds?(@source, item)

    [@infusesack, @target].any? { |container| holds?(container, item) } && take(item) && put_away(item.id, @source)
  end

  def self.holds?(container, item)
    look_in(container).any? { |obj| obj.id.to_s == item.id.to_s }
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- reading a check
  # a check is { spell number => what can be added (nil = locked) }
  def self.locked(check)
    check.select { |_num, add| add.nil? }.keys
  end

  def self.unlocked(check)
    check.reject { |_num, add| add.nil? }.keys
  end

  # the spells that can still be infused
  def self.room_left(check)
    check.select { |_num, add| add && add !~ /\Ano\b/i }.keys
  end

  def self.full?(check)
    !check.empty? && locked(check).empty? && room_left(check).empty?
  end

  def self.label(item, check = nil)
    spells = check.to_h.keys
    spells.empty? ? item.name.to_s : "#{item.name} (#{spells.join(', ')})"
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- one run of fizzfuse
  def self.kill_fizzfuse
    return unless Script.running?('fizzfuse')

    Script.kill('fizzfuse')
    wait_for(10) { !Script.running?('fizzfuse') }
    # it dies with go2 still walking if it was off making a rune
    Script.kill('go2') if Script.running?('go2')
  end

  # What one line of the game's says about the run. Returns :progress, :bad or nil.
  def self.note(run, line)
    case line
    when STATUS_START then run[:checks] << {}
    when STATUS_SPELL
      match = Regexp.last_match
      return nil if run[:checks].empty?

      run[:checks].last[match[:num].to_i] = match[:add]
    when UNLOCKED     then run[:unlocked] += 1
    when SHOOK        then run[:shook] = true
    when SHOOK_LITTLE then run[:final] = true
    when STONE_AURA   then run[:aura] = run[:final] = true
    when SCROLL_AURA  then run[:ended] = 'a white aura locked it for good'
    when EXPLODED     then run[:exploded] = true
    when WENT_COLD
      run[:infused] += 1
      run[:ended] = 'it reached its limit and locked for good'
    when INFUSED      then run[:infused] += 1
    when FULL         then run[:full] = true
    when INJURED      then run[:injured] = true
    when NO_SILVER    then run[:no_silver] = true
    when EMPTY_HANDED then return :bad
    when NO_MANA      then return checkmana < maxmana.to_i * 0.9 ? :progress : :bad
    when STRAINED, RUNE_WORK, LINKED then nil
    else return nil
    end
    :progress
  end

  # Run ;fizzfuse to the end, or kill it when it's stuck, the stone blew up or you died.
  # run[:broke] says why, when it didn't end by itself.
  def self.fizzfuse(args)
    run = { checks: [], unlocked: 0, infused: 0 }
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    Script.current.clear
    started_in = Room.current&.id
    unless Script.start('fizzfuse', args)
      run[:broke] = "couldn't start fizzfuse"
      @give_up = run[:broke]
      return run
    end

    last = Time.now
    bad = 0
    exited = nil
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line
        case note(run, line)
        when :progress
          last = Time.now
          bad = 0
        when :bad
          bad += 1
        end
        run[:broke] = 'the stone exploded' if run[:exploded]
        run[:broke] = 'it was waving or infusing with nothing in hand' if bad >= 5
      end
      break if run[:broke]
      next if line

      # only once every line is read: the explosion's own line comes before the death's
      if dead?
        run[:broke] = 'you died'
        break
      end
      # the last replies can land after it has exited
      exited ||= Time.now unless Script.running?('fizzfuse')
      break if exited && Time.now - exited > 1.0

      last = Time.now if Script.running?('go2') || Script.paused?('fizzfuse') || checkmana < mana_wait
      if !exited && Time.now - last > stall_limit
        run[:broke] = "nothing happened for #{stall_limit} seconds"
        break
      end
      sleep 0.1
    end
    kill_fizzfuse
    return_to(started_in) unless dead?
    run
  end

  # killed or bailed out halfway to a shop
  def self.return_to(room)
    return if room.nil? || wait_for(1) { Room.current&.id == room }

    Script.run('go2', room.to_s)
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- health
  # after an explosion (force), bleeding, or hurt. False when it's no use going on.
  def self.recover(force: false)
    wait_for(120) { !stunned? || dead? }
    return false if dead?

    waitrt?
    return true unless force || checkbleeding || Char.percent_health < heal_below

    room = Room.current&.id
    msg "#{Char.percent_health}% health#{', bleeding' if checkbleeding}: running eherbs."
    if Script.start('eherbs')
      wait_for(600) { !Script.running?('eherbs') || dead? }
      Script.kill('eherbs') if Script.running?('eherbs')
    end
    return false if dead?

    return_to(room)
    return true unless checkbleeding || Char.percent_health < stop_below

    @give_up = "you're still hurt after eherbs (#{Char.percent_health}% health#{', bleeding' if checkbleeding})"
    false
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- one scroll
  # A run that ended badly: put things back, and stop everything after the second in a row.
  def self.trouble(item, why)
    @bad_in_a_row += 1
    home = bring_home(item)
    why = "#{why}; it's not in the #{@source.name}, look for it" unless home || dead?
    msg "#{item.name}: #{why}."
    @skipped << "#{item.name} (#{why})"
    recover(force: @last_run.to_h[:injured]) unless dead?
    @give_up ||= 'that was two scrolls in a row that went wrong' if @bad_in_a_row >= 2
  end

  def self.why(run)
    return run[:broke] if run[:broke]
    return 'you were too injured to cast Scroll Infusion' if run[:injured]
    return "there wasn't enough silver in the bank for a runestone" if run[:no_silver]

    "fizzfuse stopped before it was done"
  end

  # Nothing to read on it (some papers aren't scrolls): put it back and go on.
  def self.unreadable(item)
    @bad_in_a_row = 0
    bring_home(item)
    msg "#{item.name}: there's nothing on it to infuse, leaving it alone."
    @skipped << "#{item.name} (nothing on it)"
  end

  def self.destroyed(item)
    bold "#{item.name}: the stone exploded and destroyed it."
    @destroyed << item.name.to_s
    @bad_in_a_row = 0
    sleep 2 # for the stun or the death to show
    clear_hands if recover(force: true)
  end

  # ;fizzfuse check, which puts the scroll in `container`. Nil if it went wrong, {} if there's
  # nothing on it.
  def self.check(item, container, name)
    2.times do
      return nil unless take(item)

      run = fizzfuse("check #{cont(name)}")
      @last_run = run
      return nil if run[:broke]

      put_away(item.id, container) if in_hand?(item)
      return run[:checks].last unless run[:checks].empty?

      bring_home(item) # it never waved
    end
    nil
  end

  # ;fizzfuse infuse until nothing can take more, starting with it in the right hand. Leaves it
  # in `container` and returns what happened, or nil if it went wrong.
  def self.infuse(item, container, name)
    total = 0
    ended = nil
    final = nil
    infuse_tries.times do |try|
      unless try.zero?
        msg "#{label(item, final)}: #{room_left(final).join(', ')} can still take more, going again."
        return nil unless take(item)
      end
      run = fizzfuse("infuse #{cont(name)}")
      @last_run = run
      total += run[:infused]
      ended = run[:ended] || ended
      return nil if run[:broke] || run[:checks].empty?

      final = run[:checks].last
      # it checks again when it's done, unless there was nothing to do
      return nil if run[:checks].size < 2 && !full?(final)
      return nil if in_hand?(item) && !put_away(item.id, container)
      break if room_left(final).empty? || ended
    end
    { check: final, infused: total, ended: ended }
  end

  # --- with no arguments
  def self.top_up(item)
    found = check(item, @source, @source_name)
    if found.nil?
      return if dead?
      return trouble(item, "it couldn't be checked: #{why(@last_run.to_h)}")
    end
    return unreadable(item) if found.empty?

    if room_left(found).empty?
      @bad_in_a_row = 0
      if locked(found).size == found.size
        @locked << label(item, found)
        msg "#{label(item, found)}: locked, leaving it alone."
      else
        @already << label(item, found)
        msg "#{label(item, found)}: nothing to add#{", #{locked(found).join(', ')} locked" unless locked(found).empty?}."
      end
      return
    end

    msg "#{label(item, found)}: infusing #{room_left(found).join(', ')}."
    done = take(item) && infuse(item, @source, @source_name)
    finish(item, done)
  end

  # --- with a source and a target
  def self.tend(item)
    return trouble(item, "it couldn't be picked up") unless take(item)

    case unlock(item)
    when :destroyed then return destroyed(item)
    when :trouble   then return dead? ? nil : trouble(item, why(@last_run))
    when :blank     then return unreadable(item)
    when :stored
      @bad_in_a_row = 0
      put_away(item.id, @target) if in_hand?(item)
      @already << label(item, @last_run[:checks].first)
      return msg("#{label(item, @last_run[:checks].first)}: already unlocked and full, now in the #{@target.name}.")
    when :nothing
      @bad_in_a_row = 0
      bring_home(item)
      @stuck << label(item, @last_run[:checks].first)
      return msg("#{label(item, @last_run[:checks].first)}: nothing on it would unlock, back in the #{@source.name}.")
    when :partly
      # an aura can lock the ones that were unlocked, so look before infusing
      found = check(item, @source, @source_name)
      if found.nil?
        return if dead?
        return trouble(item, "it couldn't be checked: #{why(@last_run.to_h)}")
      end
      if unlocked(found).empty?
        @bad_in_a_row = 0
        @stuck << label(item, found)
        return msg("#{label(item, found)}: it's locked again, left in the #{@source.name}.")
      end
      msg "#{label(item, found)}: #{locked(found).join(', ')} wouldn't unlock, infusing the rest."
      return trouble(item, "it couldn't be picked up") unless take(item)
    end
    finish(item, infuse(item, @target, @target_name))
  end

  # ;fizzfuse unlock until it's done. :clean (all of it), :partly (some, and the rest won't),
  # :nothing, :stored (it was full already and fizzfuse put it in the target), :blank,
  # :destroyed or :trouble. The scroll is in the right hand after the first three.
  def self.unlock(item)
    barren = 0
    loop do
      run = fizzfuse("unlock #{cont(@target_name)}")
      @last_run = run
      return :destroyed if run[:exploded]
      return :trouble if run[:broke] || run[:checks].empty?

      before = run[:checks].first
      return :blank if before.empty?
      return :stored if full?(before)
      return :trouble unless in_hand?(item)

      left = locked(before).size - run[:unlocked]
      return :clean if left <= 0 && !run[:aura]
      # it should have waved, and none of the replies came back
      return :trouble unless run[:shook] || run[:final] || run[:unlocked].positive?

      barren = run[:unlocked].positive? ? 0 : barren + 1
      if run[:final] || barren >= unlock_tries
        return unlocked(before).size + run[:unlocked] > 0 ? :partly : :nothing
      end

      msg "#{label(item, before)}: #{count(left, 'spell')} still locked, trying again."
      return :trouble unless take(item)
    end
  end

  def self.finish(item, done)
    if done.nil? || done == false
      return if dead?
      return trouble(item, why(@last_run.to_h))
    end

    @bad_in_a_row = 0
    notes = [count(done[:infused], 'infusion')]
    notes << done[:ended] if done[:ended]
    unless done[:ended]
      notes << "#{room_left(done[:check]).join(', ')} not full" unless room_left(done[:check]).empty?
      notes << "#{locked(done[:check]).join(', ')} locked" unless locked(done[:check]).empty?
    end
    text = "#{label(item, done[:check])}: #{notes.join('; ')}"
    @done << text
    msg "#{text}. Now in the #{@target.name}."
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the run
  def self.usage
    respond "[scrolltender #{VERSION}]"
    respond "    ;scrolltender                    check every scroll in your scrollsack (#{UserVars.scrollsack || 'not set'})"
    respond "                                     and infuse the ones that can take more"
    respond "    ;scrolltender <source> <target>  unlock and infuse every scroll in <source>,"
    respond "                                     finished ones go in <target> (worn containers;"
    respond "                                     put quotes around a two-word name)"
  end

  def self.worn(name, what)
    container = find_container(name)
    msg "You aren't wearing a container called \"#{name}\" (#{what})." unless container
    container
  end

  def self.setup(names)
    sack = UserVars.scrollsack.to_s.strip
    pouch = UserVars.infusesack.to_s.strip
    if sack.length < 3 || pouch.length < 3
      msg 'fizzfuse needs both ;vars set scrollsack=<container> and ;vars set infusesack=<container>.'
      return false
    end
    @source_name, @target_name = names.empty? ? [sack, sack] : names
    @source     = worn(@source_name, 'the scrolls') or return false
    @target     = worn(@target_name, 'where they go') or return false
    @infusesack = worn(pouch, 'your infusesack') or return false
    if Script.running?('fizzfuse')
      msg 'fizzfuse is already running.'
      return false
    end
    true
  end

  def self.main
    # Lich keeps this module and its @variables between runs
    instance_variables.each { |var| remove_instance_variable(var) }
    @done      = []
    @already   = []
    @locked    = []
    @stuck     = []
    @destroyed = []
    @skipped   = []
    @opened    = []
    @bad_in_a_row = 0

    names = Array(Script.current.vars[1..-1]).map { |name| name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '') }.reject(&:empty?)
    return usage unless names.empty? || (names.size == 2 && names.none? { |name| name =~ /\A-/ })
    return unless setup(names)

    before_dying { ScrollTender.cleanup }
    if Script.running?('go4invoker') && !Script.paused?('go4invoker')
      Script.pause('go4invoker')
      @paused_invoker = true
      msg 'Paused go4invoker until this is done.'
    end
    if right_id || left_id
      empty_hands
      @emptied = true
      return msg("Couldn't empty your hands.") unless wait_for(3) { right_id.nil? && left_id.nil? }
    end

    # fizzfuse closes whatever it had to open; opened here first, they stay open
    look_in(@infusesack)
    look_in(@target) unless names.empty?
    scrolls = look_in(@source).select { |obj| scroll?(obj) }
    return msg("No scrolls in the #{@source.name}.") if scrolls.empty?

    @started = Time.now
    msg "#{count(scrolls.size, 'scroll')} in the #{@source.name}#{", finished ones go in the #{@target.name}" unless names.empty?}."
    scrolls.each_with_index do |item, index|
      break if dead? || @give_up
      break unless recover

      msg "#{index + 1} of #{scrolls.size}: #{item.name}"
      @current = item
      names.empty? ? top_up(item) : tend(item)
      @current = nil
      @reached = index + 1
    end
    summary(scrolls.size)
  end

  def self.summary(total)
    left = total - @reached.to_i
    bold "Stopped: #{dead? ? 'you died' : @give_up}. #{count(left, 'scroll')} not reached." if dead? || @give_up
    bold "Done with the #{@source.name} (#{((Time.now - @started) / 60).round} minutes)."
    {
      'Infused'                       => @done,
      'Already full'                  => @already,
      'Locked, left alone'            => @locked,
      'Would not unlock, not moved'   => @stuck,
      'DESTROYED by an explosion'     => @destroyed,
      'SKIPPED, something went wrong' => @skipped
    }.each do |heading, list|
      next if list.empty?

      respond "    #{heading} (#{list.size}):"
      list.each { |text| respond "        #{text}" }
    end
  end

  # every way out, ;k included: no fizzfuse left running, the scroll back where it came from,
  # closed containers closed again, hands as they were
  def self.cleanup
    kill_fizzfuse
    Script.unpause('go4invoker') if @paused_invoker && Script.paused?('go4invoker')
    return if dead?

    bring_home(@current) if @current
    clear_hands if @reached || @current
    @opened.each { |container| collect("close ##{container.id}", /^You (?:close|fasten)|^That is already closed/, timeout: 2) }
    fill_hands if @emptied && right_id.nil? && left_id.nil?
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "[scrolltender] cleanup: #{e.message}"
  end
end

ScrollTender.main
